From 7f4a2b1c9e3d5f80123456789abcdef0123456789 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LX-R58CH Maintainer <maintainer@example.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: add LX-R58CH V10 support

Add initial support for the LX-R58CH V10 board (compatible
"rockchip,lz-rk3588-r58ch"), an RK3588 based terminal board.

Hardware summary:
- Power: RK806 PMIC over SPI2 + RK8602/RK8603 CPU-core regulators +
  RK8602 for the NPU rail
- Display: eDP0 panel 1920x1080@60 (VOP VP2) plus an on-board
  mini-HDMI wired to the second HDMI TX (VOP VP1); both enabled
- Audio: ES8388 codec on I2S0 (multi-codecs card)
- Wireless: AMPAK AP6256 (WiFi on SDIO, Bluetooth on UART6)
- Storage: on-board eMMC (HS400)
- Misc: ILI2511 touch controller, HYM8563 RTC, AK09918 compass,
  ICM20948 IMU, 4G modem (4g-modem-platdata), PWM fan (PWM10),
  PWM backlight (PWM11), dual USB2 host + USB3.0 OTG (host mode)

The device tree is ported from the board's production 5.10 BSP
DTB (decompiled) and adapted to the 6.1 bindings: GPU compatible
is now arm,mali-valhall, the HDMI-mode PHY wrapper nodes are gone
(HDMI1 shares hdptxphy1 with DP1), the RK806 DVS pin nodes were
dropped, and display-subsystem now takes the HDMI PLL clocks.
All hardware codec blocks are enabled, including the AV1 decoder.
Ethernet controllers are kept disabled exactly as shipped by the
board vendor (config is retained for future enablement).

Boot: UART2 debug console (fiq-debugger, ttyFIQ @ 1500000).

